# Auto Assignment Solution for Incidents in ServiceNow

## Recommended Approach: **Business Rule**

Given your constraints, a **Business Rule** is the best solution as it:
- ✅ Works on both Insert & Change
- ✅ Supports Contact Type field
- ✅ Can handle all 15 combinations efficiently
- ✅ Runs server-side (reliable & fast)

---

## Business Rule Setup

```
Name: Auto Assignment - Incident Category Routing
Table: Incident [incident]
When: Before
Insert: ✅ True
Update: ✅ True
Order: 100
```

### Condition:
```javascript
current.contact_type.changesTo() || 
current.category.changesTo() || 
current.subcategory.changesTo()
```

---

## Script (Handles All 15 Combinations)

```javascript
(function executeRule(current, previous) {

    // =============================================
    // Assignment Matrix - Add all 15 combinations
    // =============================================
    var assignmentMatrix = [
        // Format: contact_type (comma-separated), category, subcategory, assignment_group
        {
            contact_type: ['web', 'email'],
            category: 'A',
            subcategory: 'B',
            group: 'test'
        },
        {
            contact_type: ['web', 'email'],
            category: 'A',
            subcategory: 'C',
            group: 'test_group_2'
        },
        {
            contact_type: ['phone'],
            category: 'B',
            subcategory: 'D',
            group: 'test_group_3'
        },
        // ➕ Add remaining combinations below...
        // Copy the block above and modify values
    ];

    // =============================================
    // Core Logic - Do Not Modify
    // =============================================
    var contactType  = current.contact_type.toString().toLowerCase();
    var category     = current.category.toString();
    var subcategory  = current.subcategory.toString();

    for (var i = 0; i < assignmentMatrix.length; i++) {
        var rule = assignmentMatrix[i];

        var contactMatch    = rule.contact_type.indexOf(contactType) !== -1;
        var categoryMatch   = rule.category === category;
        var subcategoryMatch = rule.subcategory === subcategory;

        if (contactMatch && categoryMatch && subcategoryMatch) {

            // Lookup Assignment Group sys_id
            var grpGR = new GlideRecord('sys_user_group');
            grpGR.addQuery('name', rule.group);
            grpGR.setLimit(1);
            grpGR.query();

            if (grpGR.next()) {
                current.assignment_group = grpGR.sys_id;
                gs.log('Auto Assignment Applied: Group = ' + rule.group, 'AutoAssignment');
            } else {
                gs.logWarning('Group not found: ' + rule.group, 'AutoAssignment');
            }
            break; // Stop after first match
        }
    }

})(current, previous);
```

---

## 15 Combinations Template

```javascript
var assignmentMatrix = [
    // 1
    { contact_type: ['web', 'email'], category: 'A', subcategory: 'B', group: 'test' },
    // 2
    { contact_type: ['web'], category: 'A', subcategory: 'C', group: 'Group2' },
    // 3
    { contact_type: ['email'], category: 'B', subcategory: 'D', group: 'Group3' },
    // 4
    { contact_type: ['phone'], category: 'C', subcategory: 'E', group: 'Group4' },
    // 5
    { contact_type: ['web', 'phone'], category: 'D', subcategory: 'F', group: 'Group5' },
    // 6
    { contact_type: ['email'], category: 'A', subcategory: 'G', group: 'Group6' },
    // 7
    { contact_type: ['web'], category: 'B', subcategory: 'H', group: 'Group7' },
    // 8
    { contact_type: ['phone', 'email'], category: 'C', subcategory: 'I', group: 'Group8' },
    // 9
    { contact_type: ['web'], category: 'D', subcategory: 'J', group: 'Group9' },
    // 10
    { contact_type: ['email'], category: 'E', subcategory: 'K', group: 'Group10' },
    // 11
    { contact_type: ['phone'], category: 'A', subcategory: 'L', group: 'Group11' },
    // 12
    { contact_type: ['web', 'email'], category: 'B', subcategory: 'M', group: 'Group12' },
    // 13
    { contact_type: ['phone'], category: 'C', subcategory: 'N', group: 'Group13' },
    // 14
    { contact_type: ['web'], category: 'E', subcategory: 'O', group: 'Group14' },
    // 15
    { contact_type: ['email', 'phone'], category: 'F', subcategory: 'P', group: 'Group15' },
];
```

---

## Alternative: Data-Driven Approach (Scalable)

> If combinations may grow beyond 15, use a **Custom Table** instead of hardcoding.

### Create Custom Table: `u_assignment_routing`

| Field | Type |
|-------|------|
| u_contact_type | String |
| u_category | String |
| u_subcategory | String |
| u_assignment_group | Reference → sys_user_group |

### Business Rule Script (Dynamic):

```javascript
(function executeRule(current, previous) {

    var routeGR = new GlideRecord('u_assignment_routing');
    routeGR.addQuery('u_contact_type', 'CONTAINS', 
                      current.contact_type.toString());
    routeGR.addQuery('u_category', current.category.toString());
    routeGR.addQuery('u_subcategory', current.subcategory.toString());
    routeGR.setLimit(1);
    routeGR.query();

    if (routeGR.next()) {
        current.assignment_group = routeGR.u_assignment_group;
        gs.log('Auto Assigned to: ' + 
               routeGR.u_assignment_group.getDisplayValue(), 
               'AutoAssignment');
    }

})(current, previous);
```

---

## Summary

| Approach | Best For |
|----------|----------|
| ✅ **Business Rule (Matrix)** | Fixed 15 combinations |
| ✅ **Business Rule (Custom Table)** | Dynamic/growing rules |
| ❌ Assignment Lookup Rules | No Contact Type support |
| ❌ Assignment Rules | Doesn't fire on change |

> 💡 **Recommendation**: Use the **Custom Table approach** for easy maintenance by admins without touching code.

