## Key Design Points

| Feature | Description |
|---|---|
| **Concurrency control** | At most `N` tasks run simultaneously |
| **FIFO queue** | Waiting tasks run in the order they were added |
| **Slot reuse** | A finished task immediately frees its slot for the next queued task |
| **Error isolation** | A failing task doesn't affect others; error propagates to the caller |
| **`drain()`** | Await until all tasks (running + queued) are complete |
| **`stats`** | Inspect current running/queued counts at any time |

